    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class with `@Test`) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` (GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n**New logic** \u2014 `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` in a new utility class (mirroring the existing `Locality` util): starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`MembershipLevel.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for the level computation.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` mapping (which read `householdSize`/`namesakeCount`/`email` for the tier) is replaced by a `membershipLevel` mapping delegating to `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` string enum schema is replaced by a `membershipLevel` integer field (int32, min 1, max 3), so the generated DTO/response now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n4. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (the spec called out the create audit line as something that recorded the tier and must record the level instead), reusing the same `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` to avoid duplicated logic.\n5. **`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`** \u2014 updated a now-stale comment that referenced the removed \"membership tier\" (household-stamping behaviour left intact).\n\nThe `coreNumericLevel` test (email present + `namesakeCount == 0` \u2192 level 3) passes, and the audit output confirms `membershipLevel=3` is emitted at creation.\n\nNote: `householdSize` is still computed/persisted but no longer read by anything (it previously drove the GOLD tier). I left it in place since removing the column/logic is outside this change's scope and could affect the household-sharing feature.",
